// src/std/mem/mem.zen
//
// The folder's public surface: starred re-exports, and nothing
// else. Re-export is an import whose bindings are starred, so this
// file adds no declaration of its own and the module below is free
// to move one between mem_alloc, mem_arena and mem_ptr without a
// line here changing.
//
// The law this folder carries: there is NO ambient allocator.
// Anything that needs memory takes an Alloc.
//
// A name absent from this list is module-private on purpose.
// ArenaState is the named case — what an arena is made of is not
// part of what an arena is — and so are PAGE_BYTES, HEADER_BYTES
// and align_up.

// the interface and its one failure. Everything that allocates
// takes an Alloc; there is exactly one way to run out of memory
AllocError*, Alloc* = std.mem.mem_alloc

// the implementation that owns the memory, and the page authority
// it draws from. Arena is Drop; the Alloc handle onto it is not.
// Page appears because Mem's signature names it — law 6, no
// exemptions
Arena*, Mem*, Page* = std.mem.mem_arena

// the raw floor. Zen has no pointer sigil, so a raw pointer is
// Ptr<T>, and a collection that owns nothing yet holds null_ptr<T>()
Ptr*, null_ptr* = std.mem.mem_ptr
